Key parsing functions:
- `norm(s)`: NFKC, lowercase, collapse whitespace.
- `tokens(s)`: regex `[a-z0-9]+` on NFKC-lowercased with LaTeX stripped. For matching abstract text, strip `$...$` math markers but keep content; handle `\` commands crudely.
- `strip_prefix(quote)`: remove leading "Abstract:", "arXiv abstract (via INSPIRE):", "CrossRef abstract:", "Springer abstract:", "arXiv abstract (verbatim, same as published):", quotes, leading "...".
- `title_cmp`: strip parenthetical suffix from ledger title; normalize; check exact equality or containment (fetched title in ledger title or vice versa); also handle unicode dashes.
- Authors: compare set of last names.
- Year: from fetched metadata.
- Venue: for arXiv API, journal_ref; for Crossref, container-title + volume/issue/page + issued year.

Verdict logic:
```
mech title_match == exact or containment
year_ok: fetched_year == ledger_year, or (ledger year is publication year and fetched issued year differs by <=1) -> note
excerpt coverage: cov = |ledger_tokens ∩ fetched_tokens| / |ledger_tokens| ; ordered = SequenceMatcher ratio
if not (title_exact or title_contains): MISMATCH
elif cov >= 0.9 and year_ok: MATCH
elif cov >= 0.9 and not year_ok: PARTIAL (year convention)
elif cov >= 0.5: PARTIAL
else: MISMATCH (content not supported)
```
For metadata-type rows (SRC-067): verdict from title+authors+year+venue presence.

